{"id": "EUVD-2026-59376", "enisaUuid": "15006c83-a711-3444-a34b-16f5fa0881a7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/ntfs3: call _ntfs_bad_inode() when failing to rename\n\nIt is safe to call _ntfs_bad_inode on live inodes since:\n  commit 519b078998ce (\"fs/ntfs3: Exclude call make_bad_inode for live nodes.\")\n\nThe WARN_ON was added when it wasn't safe by:\n  commit d99208b91933 (\"fs/ntfs3: cancle set bad inode after removing name fails\")\n\nReplace the WARN_ON with a call to _ntfs_bad_inode() to prevent further\noperations on the inconsistent inode.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T10:08:45", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/580896e33003845de66c75cd61544cf9d9bfbe15", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff825bf0521f6da2f30878cbad18ab7b341bc31b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8ed78f40eecd0176fda71d673f6957c98e7ffbe"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9679-5mjr-46x9", "CVE-2026-72477"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.65, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20bc943b-3830-3d64-824c-7873da4dd72c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "519b078998ce6e729f98dccf35505b4756985d11 <ff825bf0521f6da2f30878cbad18ab7b341bc31b"}, {"id": "32a6c29c-1df5-3026-99f1-611b133c8965", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3b65d0e8-a0a0-34c0-ab5b-ca30d3bf85a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "415312f5-86ce-3cb3-8566-1c9bdf4e3408", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "4a697e4a-7205-3beb-bf3c-2b98499ec265", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "519b078998ce6e729f98dccf35505b4756985d11 <e8ed78f40eecd0176fda71d673f6957c98e7ffbe